  "purpose": "The hostile-monitor attempts of anchor's breach images (M11-7; planning/mvp-m11-plan.md, D-10's VS-domain column): HS code on one VS-domain hart, after its activation, attempts each target D-10 names with each kind of access and call, and records each one's trap. breach-g0 hooks hart 1 (VS domain 0, host_t), breach-g1 hart 2 (VS domain 1, prot_t); the rows are VS domain 0's, and g1 replaces the rows its rights change. own and other are the hooked VS domain and the other one. Each row's at is the physical target; tools/gen-breach.py makes the access's address from it by the row's mode.",
  "trust": "Test data. tools/gen-breach.py checks every row against the hooked image's descriptor (an outcome of denied needs a right the profile lacks, allowed every right it needs) and refuses two rows whose written or read bytes meet.",
  "scope": "anchor's breach-g0, breach-g1, and their -off copies, which make only the rows with a witness.",
